                    ]
                ]
            }
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "size": "H3",
            "content": "By using three variable K-Map, you can get the simplified expression for next state, Q(t + 1). The three variable K-Map for next state, Q(t + 1) is shown in the following figure."
        },
        {
            "type": "widget",
            "sub_type": "image",
            "content": {
                "link": "/assets/images/jk_3_variable_kmap.jpg"
            }
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "size": "H3",
            "content": "The maximum possible groupings of adjacent ones are already shown in the figure. Therefore, the simplified expression for next state Q(t+1) is"
        },
        {
            "type": "widget",
            "sub_type": "clipboard",
            "content": "          Q(t + 1) = J.Q(t)' + K'.Q(t)"
        },
        {
