        {
            "type": "text",
            "size": "H2",
            "content": "Race-Around Condition"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "size": "H3",
            "content": "In a standard JK flip-flop with J=1, K=1, the output toggles as long as the clock is HIGH. If the clock pulse is wide enough, the output feeds back and toggles multiple times in one clock cycle — this is the race around condition. Master-slave solves this by separating the capture (master, positive edge) from the output (slave, negative edge)."
